-- UKMLA Ophthalmology batch 1
-- 50 questions: acute visual loss, eyelid & lacrimal disease,
-- ocular trauma & emergencies, paediatric ophthalmology & squint,
-- red eye & ocular inflammation

  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 74-year-old woman presents with sudden painless loss of vision in her right eye over the last hour. For the past three weeks she has had a persistent right-sided headache, scalp tenderness when brushing her hair, and pain in her jaw when chewing. She has lost 3 kg in weight. On examination, visual acuity in the right eye is reduced to counting fingers, the right optic disc is pale and swollen, and the temporal artery is thickened and non-pulsatile. Blood tests show ESR 88 mm/h and CRP 62 mg/L.',
  'What is the most appropriate immediate management?',
  array['giant cell arteritis','AION','temporal arteritis','visual loss']
),
