  'draft', 'core',
  $x$A 27-year-old woman with a body mass index of 34 kg/m^2 presents with a six-week history of daily headaches, worse in the mornings, and intermittent blurring of vision in both eyes with occasional brief 'greying out' of vision on standing. She takes the combined oral contraceptive pill. Visual acuity is preserved at 6/6 bilaterally, but fundoscopy shows bilateral optic disc swelling. Neurological examination is otherwise normal.$x$,
  'What is the most appropriate next investigation?',
  array['papilloedema','idiopathic intracranial hypertension','raised ICP']
),
