  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 76-year-old woman underwent uncomplicated cataract surgery on her left eye four days ago. She now presents with increasing pain, redness and reduced vision in that eye over the last 24 hours. Visual acuity has dropped from 6/9 immediately post-op to counting fingers. On examination there is marked conjunctival injection, a hazy cornea, and a visible layer of white cells (hypopyon) in the anterior chamber. She feels systemically unwell with a low-grade fever.',
  'What is the most appropriate immediate action?',
  array['endophthalmitis','post-operative infection','ocular emergency']
),
