  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 54-year-old woman presents with a several-month history of bilateral gritty, burning eyes that are worse in the morning, with crusting of the eyelashes on waking. She has mild redness of both lid margins with visible dilated blood vessels along the lash line and some flaking skin at the base of her lashes. Visual acuity is normal and there is no photophobia.',
  'What is the most appropriate first-line management?',
  array['blepharitis','lid margin disease','dry eye']
),
