  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 38-year-old man presents with a two-week history of a painless, firm lump in the upper eyelid of his left eye. There is no redness or tenderness, and vision is unaffected. On examination, a firm, round, mobile nodule is palpable within the tarsal plate, not attached to the skin, with mild eversion of the lid revealing a small area of conjunctival granulation over the lump.',
  'What is the most likely diagnosis and appropriate initial management?',
  array['chalazion','meibomian cyst','eyelid lump']
),
