  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 24-year-old woman presents with a two-day history of a painful, red swelling at the margin of her right upper eyelid, close to the base of the lashes. On examination there is a tender, erythematous pustule pointing outwards at the lash line. There is no proptosis, and eye movements are full and painless.',
  'What is the most appropriate initial management?',
  array['hordeolum','stye','eyelid infection']
),
