  'draft', 'foundation',
  'An 82-year-old man presents with a several-month history of a gritty, irritable left eye and intermittent blurred vision. On examination, the lower eyelid margin is rotated inwards so that the lashes rub against the cornea, and there is mild corneal punctate staining with fluorescein. There is no history of trauma or previous eyelid surgery.',
  'What is the most likely diagnosis?',
  array['entropion','eyelid malposition','corneal irritation']
),
('cf000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000015', 'ukmla', '4c10444b-5ef9-40a3-a1cc-646558fce13b',
  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 79-year-old woman with a history of a right-sided facial nerve palsy following removal of an acoustic neuroma three months ago presents with persistent watering and soreness of her right eye. On examination, the lower right eyelid margin is turned outward, away from the globe, with visible conjunctival injection and mild punctate staining of the lower cornea.',
  'What is the most likely diagnosis?',
  array['ectropion','facial nerve palsy','epiphora']
),
('cf000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000016', 'ukmla', '4c10444b-5ef9-40a3-a1cc-646558fce13b',
  'draft', 'core',
  'A 7-year-old boy presents with a two-day history of swelling and redness of his left upper and lower eyelids following an insect bite on the eyebrow. He is otherwise well, afebrile, and eating normally. On examination there is marked erythematous swelling of both eyelids, but the eye opens with gentle separation, visual acuity is normal, pupil reactions are normal, and eye movements are full and pain-free with no proptosis.',
