  'draft', 'core',
  'A 6-year-old girl presents to the emergency department with a one-day history of worsening swelling around her right eye, associated with fever of 38.9C and reduced appetite. She had a cold with nasal congestion last week. On examination there is marked erythematous swelling of the right eyelids, the eye is proptosed, eye movements are painful and restricted in all directions, and visual acuity is reduced compared with the left eye.',
  'What is the most appropriate immediate management?',
  array['orbital cellulitis','sinusitis','paediatric emergency']
),
