  'draft', 'core',
  'A 45-year-old man is brought to the emergency department after a metal fragment flew into his left eye while he was using an angle grinder without eye protection. He describes sudden sharp pain and reports that his vision has become very blurred. On examination there is a small full-thickness laceration visible at the corneal margin, the anterior chamber appears shallow, and the pupil is irregular and peaked towards the wound.',
