  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 50-year-old man attends the emergency department after being poked in the eye by a branch while gardening two hours ago. He has mild discomfort but reports his vision is normal. On examination there is a well-demarcated, bright red patch of blood beneath the conjunctiva over the lateral sclera, with no visible laceration, normal visual acuity, a normal pupil, and a fully visible posterior extent of the haemorrhage on examination.',
  'What is the most appropriate management?',
  array['subconjunctival haemorrhage','minor ocular trauma','red flag assessment']
),
